                {
                  "id": "code-threat-008",
                  "title": "Mock User Header Injection Detection",
                  "status": "Open",
                  "severity": "Medium",
                  "type": "Spoofing",
                  "description": "Development mode check (NODE_ENV === 'development') can be bypassed if environment variables are misconfigured or if the check uses loose equality. Additionally, even in non-development mode, the fallback in verify() accepts development user if useremail is undefined and NODE_ENV check fails.",
                  "mitigation": "Use strict equality (===) for environment checks. Remove development fallbacks entirely. Use build-time Constants instead of runtime environment variables for security features.",
